        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// The header row for the Inbox tab.\n//\n// FOUR control columns since 2026-08-29, and they sit first so staff can paste an export straight\n// to their right without touching them. Everything further right is whatever the source gave them\n// — the mapper reads those headers and works out what they mean.\n//\n// `status` is the claim marker: blank means unprocessed. That is the same convention every other\n// polling workflow here uses, so a row is claimed by its own state rather than a separate lock.\n//\n// `Product` is the one column staff MUST fill themselves, and it is capital-P to match the live\n// Leads tab. Nothing can infer it: `source_config` records how a lead arrived (Apollo /\n// Warmly-Intent / Referral / Manual), which says nothing about whether this person should hear\n// from OryonIQ or from VisioneerIT. A blank refuses the row rather than guessing, because a wrong\n// guess sends the wrong company's pitch to a real person. Put a data-validation dropdown on this\n// column offering exactly: OryonIQ, VisioneerIT.\nreturn [{ json: { status: '', notes: '', mapped_lead_id: '', Product: '',\n                  'First name': '', 'Last name': '', 'Company name': '',\n                  'Email address': '', 'Website': '' } }];"
      },
